>> title: Pot Roast, Slow Cooker
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: beef, sunday dinner, braise, one-pot, slow cooker, crock pot
>> counters: The Slow Cooker
>> dish: pot-roast
>> kit: Slow Cooker
>> aka: yankee pot roast, hot beef commercial, hot beef sandwich, slow cooker pot roast, crockpot pot roast, crock pot roast
>> servings: 6
>> time: 8 hr 40 min
>> slack: forgiving — chuck that is tender at seven hours is only more tender at ten; the potatoes give out first, and in a crock they were always going to be soft
>> step.2: rub, both faces
>> step.3: sear 12 min in a skillet, every face
>> step.4: soften, deglaze the skillet clean
>> step.5: braise on low, 8 hr
>> step.6: thicken on high, lid off

Written for low, eight hours, which is a day you leave and come back to. Half the liquid the oven version takes, because nothing evaporates under this lid: three cups going in is three cups plus whatever the vegetables give up coming out, and that is soup with a roast in it.

Rub @beef chuck roast{4%lb}(1.8 kg) with @kosher salt{1%Tbs}, @black pepper{1%tsp}.

Sear @&(~1)seasoned roast{} in @vegetable oil{2%Tbs} in a #skillet{} for ~sear{12%min}, turning it onto every face including the ends. The machine cannot do this and there is no later step that makes up for it — a roast that goes in pale comes out pale.

Soften @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced), @garlic{4%cloves}, @tomato paste{2%Tbs} in the same skillet with @&(~1)seared roast{}, then pour in @dry red wine{1/2%cup}(120 mL) and scrape until nothing is stuck to the base, which is the only place that flavour exists.

Slow cook @&(~1)pot{} with @beef stock{1%cup}(240 mL), @thyme{4%sprigs}, @carrots{1%lb}(450 g; cut in 2-in lengths), @Yukon Gold potatoes{2%lb}(900 g; halved) in a #slow cooker{} on low for ~slow cook{8%hr}, lid on and left alone — every lift costs about twenty minutes of recovery, and the point of the day is that you are not there to lift it.

Thicken @&(~1)pot roast{} on high with the lid off, stirring in @cornstarch{2%Tbs}(16 g; slaked in 2 Tbs cold water) for ~thicken{20%min}, the roast lifted out and resting under foil. The oven version reduces on its own for four hours; this one has to be told to.
